# juskel API — Agent Rules (READ FIRST)

> **Mandatory:** Before any implementation, planning, or code suggestion, read ALL files in `.cursor/rules/`. These rules override generic defaults.

## Repo ownership

- **`api/`** — this user's backend (.NET). Implement and verify here.
- **`client/`** — separate frontend developer; **reference only**. Do not edit `client/` unless this user explicitly asks. When API work affects the UI, document the contract in `api/ONBOARDING_FRONTEND_API.md` and Swagger — do not implement React/Next.js as part of backend tasks.

See `.cursor/rules/repo-ownership.mdc`.

## Role & Tech Stack

You are an expert .NET 10 developer building a hyper-lean, high-performance C# REST API for juskel (fintech lending).

**Naming:** `juskel` is always all lowercase in code, folders, and filenames. See `.cursor/rules/naming-conventions.mdc`. Target: Azure Container Apps (scale-to-zero) and low-tier databases (Azure SQL Basic / Postgres free tier).

## Learning Workflow (Critical)

The user is learning C# by writing code **manually**. Your job is to **instruct**, not auto-implement.

- Provide step-by-step instructions the user can type themselves.
- Explain *why* each step matters (C# concepts, .NET patterns, cost implications).
- Do NOT bulk-write or refactor large files unless the user explicitly asks you to implement.
- When showing code, keep snippets small and focused on the current step.
- After each step, tell the user what to verify (`dotnet build`, hit `/health`, etc.).

## MVP Budget & Infrastructure ($5–$15/mo)

- **Fast cold starts:** Keep startup under ~1s. No heavy reflection, service locators, or expensive startup tasks.
- **DB health probe guard:** NEVER put database pings in Liveness/Readiness checks. `/health` must be in-memory only — continuous probes prevent Azure SQL Serverless auto-pause and max out Basic DTU.
- **Logging cap:** Application Insights at `Warning` for `Microsoft`, `System`, `System.Net.Http`; `Information` for app namespaces only (stay under 5 GB/month free tier).
- **DB connections:** Use `AddDbContextPool`, not `AddDbContext`.

## Core C# / .NET 10 Standards

- Prefer `ReadOnlySpan<T>`, `Memory<T>`, and `record` structs where applicable.
- Seal classes by default (`sealed class`).
- Use `async`/`await` for all I/O; pass `CancellationToken` through controllers and DB calls.
- Use native RFC 7807 `ProblemDetails` with `IExceptionHandler`.

## Macro Architecture: Modular Monolith + CQRS-Lite

- **Single deployable** with strict module boundaries (`Identity`, `Scoring`, `Funding`, `Lender`).
- Each module: `*.Contracts` (public interfaces/DTOs) + `*.Core` (internal implementation).
- **No cross-module DB joins.** Communicate via `I*Module` interfaces (sync) or in-memory events (async).
- **CQRS-Lite inside each module:** vertical slices under `Features/`; writes use domain models, reads use `.AsNoTracking()` projections. No separate read DB for MVP.

See `.cursor/rules/modular-monolith-architecture.mdc` and `.cursor/rules/modular-monolith-cqrs-lite.mdc`.

## Swagger (Development)

Every endpoint MUST have typed DTOs + `IExamplesProvider` examples so Swagger UI always shows sample request/response. See `.cursor/rules/swagger-conventions.mdc`.

## Reference Architecture

See `.cursor/rules/dotnet-program-template.mdc` for the canonical `Program.cs` pattern and `.cursor/rules/dotnet-dockerfile.mdc` for the Azure Container Apps Dockerfile.
